# Veritas Talker Engine

Wine shelf talker designer and print PDF generator. Private repo: https://github.com/Hyper217/veritas-talker-engine

## Current phase

Phase 1 — Build Hardening. See `ROADMAP.md` for the single source of truth. Do not start Phase 2+ until exit criteria are met. Desktop `.exe` (Tauri) is Phase 4 — last.

## Tech stack

- React 19 + TypeScript + Vite 6 (ESM, `type: "module"`)
- Tailwind CSS 4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`
- TipTap (rich text), html2canvas + jsPDF (PDF), Motion (animations)
- Lucide React icons
- Local storage only — no backend, no cloud required

## Dev commands

- `npm run dev` — port **3001** (intentional; avoids localhost clashes)
- `npm run build` / `npm run preview` — production on port 4173
- `npm run lint` — `tsc --noEmit` only

## Architecture

```
src/
├── App.tsx              # Main UI, catalog, queue, PDF orchestration
├── components/          # ShelfTalker, LayoutEditor, RichTextEditor, Toast, FitText
├── lib/                 # pdf.ts, flowLayout.ts, talkerDimensions.ts, utils.ts
└── types.ts             # Product, AppSettings, FlowZone, DesignLayout
```

**Layouts:** Noir (built-in black & gold) + Google Flow imports only. Classic/Bento/Heritage/Botanical were removed — do not reintroduce.

**Flow workflow:** Design in Google Flow (3:4 portrait) → export PNG → import via Sparkles panel → zone overlays at print time. No Flow API exists.

## Print constraints

- Talker size: 4×5 inches (384×510 px constants in `types.ts`)
- 2×2 grid per US Letter sheet; queues >4 wines span multiple pages
- PDF uses sequential html2canvas capture at scale 3 — preserve exact dimensions, no stretch
- Chrome/Edge produce best PDF output
- Remote images need CORS; Dropbox links and drag-drop always work
- html2canvas cannot render oklch colors — `pdf.ts` has a fixOklchColors workaround

## Coding preferences

- Minimize scope — smallest correct diff; don't add unrelated features
- Match existing patterns: functional React, `useCallback`/`useMemo` where already used
- Types live in `types.ts`; print constants in `talkerDimensions.ts`
- Data migrations: follow `migrateSettings` / `migrateDesignLayout` patterns for localStorage
- Only add tests or docs when explicitly requested
- Never commit secrets; catalog/settings are localStorage only

## Git

- Branch: `master`
- Git hooks installed via `postinstall` (version bump script)
- Do not force-push to master
